WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions describe only what is on screen. Recorded on production,
proof.noetfield.com, 2026-08-06. One continuous take, no cuts, no
re-creation. The run in this recording is the run that happened.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
The Evidence Lab. The engine runs in the
viewer's own request — nothing pre-recorded.

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.600
Five acts: two blocked deployments, one issued
token, a hundred runs, and a refusal.

3
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.800
Act 1. An AI export writes straight to the
production database.

4
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:12.400
Eight gates run. G4 fails.
EXIT 20 — the deploy token is withheld.

5
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.600
Act 2. The database call is fixed, but an AWS
key ships in the config. EXIT 40 — escalated.

6
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.800
Act 3. A clean artifact clears all eight gates.
A short-lived token is minted.

7
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:19.600
The token is bound to that artifact's exact hash.

8
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.400
Act 4. One hundred runs, with paths, timestamps,
file order, locale and timezone perturbed.

9
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:22.600
One distinct verdict hash across all one hundred.

10
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:23.800
Then six negative controls. Every one moves the
hash — proving it is sensitive, not constant.

11
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.400
Act 5. One byte is added, and the same
still-valid token is presented again.

12
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.600
REFUSED. The artifact changed, so it deploys nothing.

13
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:31.300
Intake replaces the pull request. Verification
replaces CI. Execution replaces the merge button.
